#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfc862ea-961c-50e4-a89b-10c5ef88d851" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "08a55503-97c4-5987-8c97-71990b6c2cbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-3220" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 9?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $x^2+y^2=9$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =9 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\ r & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nIn conclusion, the circle is centered at the origin and its radius is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31d92381-0c28-53fc-b918-99c16544c201" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "5382cb24-6a11-51a5-bc80-5cfed0412870" :question/math-academy-id "e-3221" :question/problem "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/6d437677c2ae4c642a30ccf3528ab390274137d8ec646731aaf3b8a024e649da.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and has radius $r = 2.$ So, the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30bb1401-f704-520c-a23e-5a238e44960e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "f7713cee-abb9-5ac6-bf69-7ddc7c14e3fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-3223" :question/problem "Which equation describes the set of all points $(x,y)$ in the coordinate plane that are a distance of $4$ from the origin?" :question/worked-solution "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance $4$ from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=4$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/8ce0e0d4582e98c15c0baea65910d03d7877550d2647581adff04df65e643e9c.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "4a9af9d3-13b3-5510-a46e-5babac13cd40" :question/math-academy-id "e-3225" :question/problem "Given that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(-2,4)$ and $(2,-4),$ respectively,  lie on a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/1909e28f4fa0376eb59fc1d1a117d10e9fbe4580aee1706e90516d84dede5940.png)" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nNow, we first calculate the diameter $AB\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{(-2-2)^{2}+{(4-(-4))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overline{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{AB}{2} = \\dfrac {4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt5.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfc862ea-961c-50e4-a89b-10c5ef88d851" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecd621df-259c-5ab7-b4f2-37364568cbb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300222} {:answer/id #uuid "46e4a611-a047-562d-b22b-561da3e16df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300223} {:answer/id #uuid "df159787-1b6d-5aad-b1f3-6f57e4e21fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,2)$ and the radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300224} {:answer/id #uuid "a250b950-8fa6-52d9-878d-8a2b2312a788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,2)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300225} {:answer/id #uuid "2784d62a-f4bf-562a-9e59-35592c9bfb8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46e4a611-a047-562d-b22b-561da3e16df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300223} :answer-field/id #uuid "f02eb77d-ff25-5359-af01-58e5c835c0e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6ef5e6f3-6c45-5d98-acf4-10fcf48b2036" :question/math-academy-id "q-116907" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =2 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e35d3d6a-3b91-51ad-9f88-38c2843cdc6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300229} {:answer/id #uuid "db0fd51e-e76c-555f-9699-f32217b057e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300230} {:answer/id #uuid "528eb12a-a74e-5b28-a070-e12a4489bd19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300231} {:answer/id #uuid "333f8e35-2f38-5923-9acf-51563f336b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300232} {:answer/id #uuid "a9382ecc-1a07-53cc-a109-22b49f37bfc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db0fd51e-e76c-555f-9699-f32217b057e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300230} :answer-field/id #uuid "2486e628-9311-5fb6-8e2b-19781c671d57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6871bb55-7096-5bdc-95c3-97647e61a9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-116927" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/343897550f0f7b9e4a479e47c9191ababa31070dac79dbf4d54befe869661a48.png)\n\nGiven that the points $X$ and $Y$ with coordinates $(-1,2)$ and $(1,-2),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{XY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-1)^{2}+(2-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6778cf3d-0306-556d-9879-566cfa0f6f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300236} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c1258b-cb57-5a5d-97f3-d3a123597d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300237} {:answer/id #uuid "0f919697-d086-5c01-b28c-dab3ff23bcf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300238} {:answer/id #uuid "fea0b4b6-4011-5789-a704-3774e3fbe460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300239} {:answer/id #uuid "d30a2377-bc5d-52ea-a655-ebf7df3b76b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea0b4b6-4011-5789-a704-3774e3fbe460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300239} :answer-field/id #uuid "021ccf57-4059-55f5-b193-fcbb451d844e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08a7411b-9289-5682-bc33-79fdf3eacff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-14559" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/14af607cba7a2c47e8443857f5f3ed6ff33cd5fa2fb12e5d451eea08a932139a.png)\n\nGiven that the points $X$ and $Y$ with coordinates $(3,4)$ and $(-3,-4),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{XY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(3-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{10}{2}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e981f22e-f58c-5d7c-970c-347c755301b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300243} {:answer/id #uuid "50b5a42d-f6fa-5bca-9451-7cef0f9f1e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300244} {:answer/id #uuid "35437fe5-455c-59de-a3c4-8a763e0abc4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300245} {:answer/id #uuid "b03c1f53-c44f-58b7-b259-78b52929749c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300246} {:answer/id #uuid "431b9c82-735d-51c9-8fb5-193a7feed47f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b03c1f53-c44f-58b7-b259-78b52929749c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f17139a4-91d9-57e4-91f3-a7220dc96294" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24a2c657-8ab6-560c-a6d6-937a612e0a3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-14792" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/1baa0bec9c8cfdb2ce80d47e66f6ba54d34266267df3ee323a658c0f98a52f83.png)\n\nGiven that the points $X$ and $Y$ with coordinates $(1,4)$ and $(-1,-4),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{XY}:$\n  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(1-(-1))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{68} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 17} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{17}}{2}=\\sqrt{17}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{17})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc0d17fe-a39d-5eb4-9aa6-2f57718d3d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300250} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6901a4-3ef9-5f8d-b644-08f9ec6fdc02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=136" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300251} {:answer/id #uuid "123dd0d8-5abc-5a2f-929b-10e90de5c6c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300252} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6e6d10-3838-51a2-9d16-2f7fa46a3cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300253} {:answer/id #uuid "da3cc974-6abd-55b6-b5ff-4fd3d4666f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c6e6d10-3838-51a2-9d16-2f7fa46a3cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300253} :answer-field/id #uuid "65d4faee-1f44-53c8-833e-1739b9e2a04c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09c5bcf7-b483-5e27-8aa0-b6f7cbd8a4b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-14793" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/883828970a6deca7d7efdc201da679324f17ec916ba0b44b76f5af2718ead2b9.png)\n\nGiven that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(3,5)$ and $(-3,-5),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{{(5-(-5))}^{2}+{(3-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 34} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{34}}{2}=\\sqrt{34}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{34})^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b4e850b-7f62-5ba1-9827-844c782a4369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300257} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c0a7b8-d3b2-59b7-b7d0-6376e1dca3b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=122" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300258} {:answer/id #uuid "1f85e94e-18a9-59f6-a5ed-5b57945edba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=244" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300259} {:answer/id #uuid "56c88e1d-a5fa-5ef0-8cfd-40f60a27150b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=(61)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300260} {:answer/id #uuid "a65ae077-05ba-53ca-8e1f-e2dac2366304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{61}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b4e850b-7f62-5ba1-9827-844c782a4369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300257} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d41c0e-8552-5118-bf3b-7ca2d5de6d3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d66c00a8-9a9a-5616-939e-722845cb2e8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-14911" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/1023ca76971805ffc07c0397565723973a6a65359cade8d0bfbfa5a5b63f8a5c.png)\n\nGiven that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(6,5)$ and $(-6,-5),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{{(5-(-5))}^{2}+{(6-(-6))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{244} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 61} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{61}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{61}}{2}=\\sqrt{61}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{61})^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =61.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300262 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31d92381-0c28-53fc-b918-99c16544c201" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90e1d879-0c26-5f23-9815-6ef764938850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90e1d879-0c26-5f23-9815-6ef764938850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300264} :answer-field/id #uuid "033e1899-6af2-5182-a6b4-7a95bbce4845" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa4d57bf-1772-56d4-8359-8245877d0415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa4d57bf-1772-56d4-8359-8245877d0415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300266} :answer-field/id #uuid "0277f074-5de8-5e33-ada1-261d61d2dbbf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7f132bd-ef18-5b00-905c-678f3ae8d408" :question/math-academy-id "q-240607" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/a3527c741af26b2135b2d676be4f055c489cd143ec7af645445219633de9645d.png)\n\nWrite the equation of the circle given above in standard form.\n\n{{field-1}} $=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The gen