 at $(0,0)$ and has radius $r=3.$ So, the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfc862ea-961c-50e4-a89b-10c5ef88d851" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "811d23e4-6715-5da7-a123-94aca7f234aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086444} {:answer/id #uuid "139e7954-fc75-5de3-8292-f36d85c2a064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086445} {:answer/id #uuid "2137b558-4293-561c-a163-e118d35ba77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 2)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086446} {:answer/id #uuid "29b868ad-04ec-5ed8-afe0-2c4ef7f2f0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 2)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086447} {:answer/id #uuid "54c77a24-d3b2-5bd7-a01e-4f85b8765a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "139e7954-fc75-5de3-8292-f36d85c2a064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086445} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b9d3c3-c9b4-54f6-8cc9-fd18d2edaeed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c03b867-7bb8-5ab7-b225-6c4b9c7f1dfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-7509" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =10 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{10}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31d92381-0c28-53fc-b918-99c16544c201" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7014f870-170d-54d9-b7d9-412f61b11fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300337} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7b7c36-07fe-5304-a3ac-1f3745462dca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300338} {:answer/id #uuid "a4845548-44d7-5d6e-9e0b-90e4d8f7bf80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300339} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef31ba3-fec4-5829-8ec1-568364a1ebb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300340} {:answer/id #uuid "53355baa-8dad-55fa-925a-ae1203b68498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7014f870-170d-54d9-b7d9-412f61b11fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300337} :answer-field/id #uuid "6383499f-c3a3-5e06-a925-29da2e4a010d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-fi